================================================================================
SECTION 2: MATHEMATICAL FORMULATIONS & ALGORITHMS
================================================================================

2.1 Semantic Similarity Matrix
Let N = {C_1, C_2, ..., C_m} represent the set of active company nodes. Each node C_i maintains an offering vector v_i^{offer} and a seeking vector v_i^{need}.

The directional semantic match score S(C_i, C_j) between Company i's offer and Company j's seeking requirement is computed via high-dimensional cosine similarity:

S(C_i, C_j) = (v_i^{offer} . v_j^{need}) / (||v_i^{offer}|| * ||v_j^{need}||)

2.2 Valuation Parity Calculation & Gap Reconciliation
For a closed k-party trade loop L = (C_1 -> C_2 -> ... -> C_k -> C_1) with estimated node transaction values V_1, V_2, ..., V_k, the Loop Parity Ratio P(L) is defined as:

P(L) = ( min(V_i) / max(V_i) ) * 100%

If P(L) < 85%, the engine calculates a micro-deliverable value gap Delta V_i = V_max - V_i, and queries the vector index to generate a dynamic sweetener deliverable proposal to restore loop parity to P(L) >= 95%.

