================================================================================
SECTION 4: PROVISIONAL PATENT APPLICATION SPECIFICATION
================================================================================

UNITED STATES PATENT AND TRADEMARK OFFICE (USPTO)
CANADIAN INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY OFFICE (CIPO)

SYSTEM AND METHOD FOR AUTONOMOUS MULTI-PARTY BARTER LOOP DISCOVERY, SEMANTIC PARITY BALANCING, AND AI-VERIFIED ESCROW FULFILLMENT

ABSTRACT
A computer-implemented system and method for executing zero-cash, multi-party business-to-business (B2B) trade exchanges. The system ingests multimodal video pitch assets and text offers/needs from participating company nodes, converting them into high-dimensional vector embeddings. A directed graph traversal engine scans vector relationships to discover closed multilateral trade loops (A -> B -> C -> A). A valuation parity calculator evaluates edge balance across the closed loop and algorithmically generates micro-deliverable proposals to bridge valuation discrepancies. Autonomous AI negotiation agents, programmed with private company constraint policies, represent parties in real-time negotiation rooms to finalize agreements. Upon execution, an AI escrow auditor evaluates multimodal delivery proofs against contract specifications to release escrowed milestones without human intervention.

FIELD OF THE INVENTION
This invention relates generally to electronic commerce, graph-based resource allocation, and autonomous software agents, and more particularly to systems and methods for multi-party zero-cash trade loop discovery, semantic value matching, and automated escrow verification.

BACKGROUND OF THE INVENTION & TECHNICAL PROBLEM
Commercial enterprises frequently possess unutilized capacity, excess inventory, or specialized service hours while simultaneously facing capital constraints for acquiring necessary vendor services. Traditional electronic marketplaces rely heavily on bilateral (A <-> B) matching, which fails when Company A requires Company B's services, but Company B has no use for Company A's output.

There is an urgent technical need for a decentralized, graph-driven network capable of automatically detecting multi-party barter loops (A -> B -> C -> A), algorithmically equalizing value gaps, and utilizing autonomous agents to negotiate and audit deliverable fulfillments.

DETAILED DESCRIPTION OF PREFERRED EMBODIMENTS
1. Semantic Need Ingestion Engine (1536-dim vectors in PostgreSQL pgvector).
2. Directed Graph Cycle Solver & Parity Engine (k-party loop detection + sweetener proposals).
3. Autonomous Agentic Negotiation Suite (LLM agents operating on private policy matrices).
4. Multimodal AI Escrow Auditor (Automated verification of URLs, repos, logistics & media proofs).

REPRESENTATIVE PATENT CLAIMS
1. A computer-implemented method for executing zero-cash multi-party trade exchanges...
2. The method of claim 1, further comprising detecting a valuation gap and algorithmically inserting a supplementary micro-deliverable...
3. A system for autonomous trade negotiation and escrow verification...
4. The system of claim 3, wherein the multimodal delivery proofs comprise at least one of a repository URL, image asset, logistics document, or media file.
